    "http://jobs.hhs.se/en/job/stockholm/assistant_professor_tenure_track_in_strategic_marketing-968667.html": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Tenure Track, in Strategic Marketing",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Tenure Track, in Strategic Marketing Available Positions Departments Back Assistant Professor, Tenure Track, in Strategic Marketing Department of Marketing and Strategy Department of Marketing and Strategy (DMS), Stockholm School of Economics The Department of Marketing and Strategy at the Stockholm School of Economics invites applications for a tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor level in strategic marketing. Please note that this is not an open-rank search; we are specifically seeking early-career scholars for appointment at the Assistant Professor level. Your profile We are looking for candidates with a completed Ph.D. degree in Business Administration  from an accredited university or business school (EQUIS, AACSB, or AMBA). The candidate must have completed their doctoral degree prior to taking up the position. As a candidate, you should have a research background in the area of strategic marketing, such as market strategies or marketing strategies, and have an interest in conducting research that has practical implications for organizations. The successful candidate is expected to thrive in an inclusive, methodologically and theoretically pluralist research environment that aims to contribute to both academic knowledge and a better society. Candidates will have demonstrable strengths in both research and teaching. Your qualifications Candidates will have the ability to publish in top-tier peer-reviewed international journals, such as AJG (4/4*) and those on the FT50 list. This will be evidenced by publications, research pipeline, and a documented presence in the international research community. Reviewing experience from relevant journals is a merit. The candidates should have documented experience from teaching relevant courses at Bachelor and/or Master levels and must demonstrate teaching effectiveness as indicated by teaching evaluations, letters of recommendations and/or peer reviews. Experience from course directorships, designing courses, coaching student projects, and teaching in executive education are considered merits.  Teaching (in English) occurs at Bachelor, Master and Executive levels. Research and teaching are equally important and the candidate will be offered support and training in pedagogy. Finally, candidates should demonstrate an ability and willingness to undertake administrative duties and play a full part in the intellectual life of the department and school at large. Conditions The tenure track period is 6 years, conditional on successful mid-term review after 3 years. Tenure evaluation takes place before the end of year 6 (at the latest), and successful evaluation leads to conversion of the tenure-track position into a tenured associate professor position. The standard teaching load for tenure-track faculty at SSE is 40%, typically corresponding to four courses per year. This load may be halved through external research grants. As the position is partially funded by a Browaldh research stipend, it carries a reduced teaching load of 20% (typically two courses per year) throughout the tenure-track period. In teaching and research, there are ample opportunities to engage in collaboration with the wide network of partner organizations at the Stockholm School of Economics, including ABB, Accenture, Ericsson, H&M, McKinsey & Co, Scania, SEB and many others. The expected start date for the position is August 2027, but we are open to discussing alternative start dates. Salaries are competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience, and are set on an individual basis. About the Department of Marketing and Strategy The Department of Marketing and Strategy is one of six Academic Departments at the Stockholm School of Economics. The department currently consists of 9 full professors, 7 associate professors, 11 assistant professors, 2 lecturers, and 20 PhD students. The department contributes to teaching in the Bachelor, Master, PhD, MBA and Executive Education programs at SSE. The department also hosts about 35 research fellows (financed by external research grants). Research at the department covers several disciplines including Marketing, Strategic Management, and International Business, but also economic sociology, economic history, and economic geography. A variety of theoretical perspectives and research methods are thus employed. The department has a high-performance research orientation and culture. Faculty members are expected to regularly publish in top journals within their respective fields. Our tenure evaluations reflect this and rely, among other things, on the AJG and FT50 lists as indicators of research quality. Besides publishing, our faculty members also actively and successfully apply for external research grants to fund both their own research and PhD and post doc projects. How to apply The formal application is made via the SSE Varbi online platform ( https://hhs.varbi.com/what:job/jobID:968667/ ) . To be considered for the position, please submit: A cover letter articulating your fit with the position description and the department, including research interests and plans, and teaching experience/competence. A complete and up-to-date curriculum vitae. A separate document listing both published articles (if any), submitted articles (including information about journal and current status), and working papers (including information about targeted journals). Copies of representative research. Names and contact information for three academic references. To ensure that your application will receive full consideration, please submit your full application by November 1, 2026 . Inquiries Please direct any inquiries to: Professor Suvi Nenonen (Head of Department, suvi.nenonen@hhs.se) SSE HR: Ellen Falkenström (ellen.falkenstrom@hhs.se) About the Stockholm School of Economics The Stockholm School of Economics is ranked as the top business school in the Nordic and Baltic countries and enjoys a strong international reputation. World-class research forms the foundation of our educational offering, which includes Bachelor, Master, PhD, MBA, and Executive Education programs. Through creativity and collaboration, the Stockholm School of Economics provides an environment where ambitious students and accomplished researchers meet to address contemporary challenges within business and economics, particularly those concerning sustainability, diversity and innovation. Apart from delivering world class education within business and economics, SSE students are trained to be successful decision makers and leaders of the future. Our educational mission has over the years strengthened SSE students, and you can read more about it here. SSE is a member of the Stockholm Dual Career Network (SDCN) , a collaboration between universities, research institutes and companies in the Stockholm region. Through SDCN, partners of international recruits are offered professional support in establishing their careers in Sweden, including career coaching, networking opportunities, seminars and access to a broad professional network. We recognize the importance of supporting accompanying partners in international relocations and are committed to facilitating a smooth transition for the whole family. SSE is committed to a balanced gender distribution and values a variety of backgrounds and experiences among our employees. We therefore welcome all applicants regardless of their gender, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, disability, sexual orientation, age, or religion or other beliefs. We strive to have a fair and inclusive recruitment process. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment August 2027 (open for negotiation) Salary Monthly. Salaries are competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience and are set individually Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number 2026/57 Contact Suvi Nenonen Ellen Falkenström Published 11.Sep.2026 Last application date 01.Nov.2026 11:59 PM CET Share links Apply for position A career page by Grade Varbi × We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here"
    },
    "http://jobs.hhs.se/en/job/stockholm/assistant_professor_tenure_track_in_marketing_especially_retailing-968687.html": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Tenure Track, in Marketing, especially Retailing",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Tenure Track, in Marketing, especially Retailing Available Positions Departments Back Assistant Professor, Tenure Track, in Marketing, especially Retailing Department of Marketing and Strategy Department of Marketing and Strategy (DMS)/Center for Retailing (CFR), Stockholm School of Economics The Department of Marketing and Strategy at the Stockholm School of Economics invites applications for two tenure-track positions at the Assistant Professor level in marketing, especially retailing. Please note that this is not an open-rank search; we are specifically seeking early-career scholars for appointment at the Assistant Professor level. Your profile We are looking for candidates with a completed Ph.D. degree in Business Administration from an accredited university or business school (EQUIS, AACSB, or AMBA). The candidate must have completed their doctoral degree prior to taking up the position. As a candidate, you should have a research background in marketing with clear contributions in areas related to retailing (e.g., consumer behavior, strategy, analytics). You should also be interested in conducting research with practical implications for retail consumers and/or organizations. The successful candidate is expected to thrive in an inclusive, methodologically and theoretically pluralist research environment that aims to contribute to both academic knowledge and a better society. Candidates will have demonstrable strengths in both research and teaching. Your qualifications Candidates will have the ability to publish in top-tier peer-reviewed international journals, such as AJG (4/4*) and those on the FT50 list. This will be evidenced by publications, research pipeline, and a documented presence in the international research community. Reviewing experience from relevant journals is a merit. The candidates should have documented experience from teaching relevant courses at Bachelor and/or Master levels and must demonstrate teaching effectiveness as indicated by teaching evaluations, letters of recommendations and/or peer reviews. Experience from course directorships, designing courses, coaching student projects, and teaching in close collaboration with industry partners are considered merits.  Teaching (in English) occurs at Bachelor, Master and Executive levels. Research and teaching are equally important and the candidate will be offered support and training in pedagogy. Finally, candidates should demonstrate an ability and willingness to undertake administrative duties and play a full part in the intellectual life of the center, department and school at large. Conditions The tenure track period is 6 years, conditional on successful mid-term review after 3 years. Tenure evaluation takes place before the end of year 6 (at the latest), and successful evaluation leads to conversion of the tenure-track position into a tenured associate professor position. The standard teaching load for tenure-track faculty at SSE is 40%, typically corresponding to four courses per year. This load may be halved through external research grants. The position also offers an opportunity to exchange part of the teaching load for pedagogical research and development during parts of the the tenure-track period. The tenure track position is located at the Center for Retailing/The Department of Marketing and Strategy. Financed through the Antonia Ax:son Johnson Tutorial Program, the candidate will be part of the core faculty in the BSc program in Retail Management run at the Center for Retailing. As such the candidate is expected to take an active role in tutoring students and integrating companies in teaching. Teaching will be important in the position, and the candidate will be offered continuous support and training in pedagogy. The candidate is also expected to engage in industry collaborations in both teaching and research, tapping into the wide network of partners at the Center for Retailing. The expected start date for the position is August 2027, but we are open to discussing alternative start dates. Salaries are competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience, and are set on an individual basis. About the Center for Retailing The Center for Retailing (CFR) is a world-leader in business school education and academic research in retail. We advance retail as an academic field and develop future industry leaders through integrated education and research in close collaboration with the actors in the retail ecosystem. CFR delivers state-of-the-art teaching and research in retail and consumer industries. Our unique model of close collaboration with corporate partners, connects academic inquiry with real-world challenges and contributes to the development of both the retail industry and retail as an academic field. About the Department of Marketing and Strategy The Department of Marketing and Strategy is one of six Academic Departments at the Stockholm School of Economics. The department currently consists of 9 full professors, 7 associate professors, 11 assistant professors, 2 lecturers, and 20 PhD students. The department contributes to teaching in the Bachelor, Master, PhD, MBA and Executive Education programs at SSE. The department also hosts about 35 research fellows (financed by external research grants). Research at the department covers several disciplines including Marketing, Strategic Management, and International Business, but also economic sociology, economic history, and economic geography. A variety of theoretical perspectives and research methods are thus employed. The department has a high-performance research orientation and culture. Faculty members are expected to regularly publish in top journals within their respective fields. Our tenure evaluations reflect this and rely, among other things, on the AJG and FT50 lists as indicators of research quality. Besides publishing, our faculty members also actively and successfully apply for external research grants to fund both their own research and PhD and post doc projects. How to apply The formal application is made via the SSE Varbi online platform (https://hhs.varbi.com/what:job/jobID:968687/) . To be considered for the position, please submit: A cover letter articulating your fit with the position description and the department, including research interests and plans, and teaching experience/competence. A complete and up-to-date curriculum vitae. A separate document listing both published articles (if any), submitted articles (including information about journal and current status), and working papers (including information about targeted journals). Copies of representative research. Names and contact information for three academic references. To ensure that your application will receive full consideration, please submit your full application by November 1, 2026 . Inquiries Please direct any inquiries to: Professor Sara Rosengren (sara.rosengren@hhs.se) SSE HR: Ellen Falkenström (ellen.falkenstrom@hhs.se) About the Stockholm School of Economics The Stockholm School of Economics is ranked as the top business school in the Nordic and Baltic countries and enjoys a strong international reputation. World-class research forms the foundation of our educational offering, which includes Bachelor, Master, PhD, MBA, and Executive Education programs. Through creativity and collaboration, the Stockholm School of Economics provides an environment where ambitious students and accomplished researchers meet to address contemporary challenges within business and economics, particularly those concerning sustainability, diversity and innovation. Apart from delivering world class education within business and economics, SSE students are trained to be successful decision makers and leaders of the future. Our educational mission has over the years strengthened SSE students, and you can read more about it here. SSE is a member of the Stockholm Dual Career Network (SDCN) , a collaboration between universities, research institutes and companies in the Stockholm region. Through SDCN, partners of international recruits are offered professional support in establishing their careers in Sweden, including career coaching, networking opportunities, seminars and access to a broad professional network. We recognize the importance of supporting accompanying partners in international relocations and are committed to facilitating a smooth transition for the whole family. SSE is committed to a balanced gender distribution and values a variety of backgrounds and experiences among our employees. We therefore welcome all applicants regardless of their gender, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, disability, sexual orientation, age, or religion or other beliefs. We strive to have a fair and inclusive recruitment process. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment August 2027 (open for negotiation) Salary Monthly. Salaries are competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience and are set individually Number of positions 2 Full-time equivalent 100% City Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number 2026/58 Contact Suvi Nenonen Ellen Falkenström Published 11.Sep.2026 Last application date 01.Nov.2026 11:59 PM CET Share links Apply for position A career page by Grade Varbi × We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here"
    },
    "http://jobs.hhs.se/en/job/stockholm/project_manager_to_civica_at_the_stockholm_school_of_economics-968344.html": {
      "title": "Project Manager to CIVICA",
      "description": "Project Manager to CIVICA at the Stockholm School of Economics Available Positions Departments Back Project Manager to CIVICA at the Stockholm School of Economics Education Office The Education Office (EdO) is one of SSE’s Professional Services units and consists of around 58 colleagues. As a central part of the SSE journey, we support and develop key academic services for students and stakeholders across our BSc, MSc, and PhD programs. Our work spans assessment, program management, scholarships, international collaborations, academic support, central course and exam coordination, as well as degrees and certificates. About CIVICA CIVICA – The European University of Social Science- is since 2019 a European Universities Alliance funded under the Erasmus+ program, aimed at implementing and developing new forms of partnerships with nine other European universities in the field of social sciences. As the CIVICA Manager, your role is twofold (1) to be the main liaison and actor for SSE’s activities internally and towards the CIVICA network (2) to lead the exploration and preparation work to transform the CIVICA Engage Track into a European Joint Bachelor’s degree.  The ambition is to prepare the ground for a future European Bachelor’s Degree (label) . If the initiative is successful, a program manager will be recruited in the future. SSE is one of CIVICA’s founding members with Sciences Po (the alliance coordinator, France), Bocconi (Italy), The London School of Economics and Political Science (United Kingdom), Central European University (Austria and Hungary), European University Institute (Florence), Hertie School (Germany), National University of Political Studies and Public Administration (Romania), SGH Warsaw School of Economics (Poland) and IE University (Spain). Since 2019, CIVICA members have jointly developed innovative activities in education, research, outreach and civic engagement; the alliance is currently in the process of developing its long-term vision and inscription in the European Degree landscape. We offer you a management role in the CIVICA project, an international and effervescent environment, at one of the top business schools in Europe. Within the CIVICA network, you will successfully manage a strategic interplay with international key stakeholders (Higher Education Institutions, Students, corporate and societal partners) to drive and develop the CIVICA project further.  The role is positioned within our Education Office department. The role Your tasks will include, but not be limited to: Manage and lead all activities related to the implementation of the CIVICA project at SSE, such as: Identify and serve the needs of SSE’s CIVICA operations in the various work packages, in line with SSE’s international strategy. Track milestones, tasks and deliverables and be responsible for SSE’s reporting to CIVICA, Budget and financial tracking of all CIVICA operations at SSE, Be part of several work packages to guarantee progress of SSE’s CIVICA operations, including WP1, governance, Hosting and leading in-person and online meetings internally and externally. Lead the exploration and preparation work to transform the CIVICA Engage Track into a European Joint Bachelor’s degree: Become SSE’s expert on European Degree (label) by following all developments on the topic at the European level Understand the work that other European University Alliances have done to deliver European Degree (label) Establish a value proposition for the Engage Track to be transformed into a European Degree (label) for all CIVICA partners Establish a road map and plan for a pilot to transform the Engage Track into a Joint European Degree (label) in a very near future Your profile Used to being responsible for multiple processes you are well-organized as well as proactive, creative, and flexible. You thrive in emerging projects where routines and solutions need to be invented while navigating established demanding structures. You are comfortable moving projects forward, and get things done efficiently and accurately. You are self-confident and independent, used to working inclusively in diverse and international teams to achieve high goals. You are service-minded and confident in dealing with a variety of stakeholders to advance the project you represent. Qualifications Experience of successful international project management, in particular Erasmus+ or Horizon Europe Experience in the European higher education sector in developing or implementing a joint or double degree program English Meritorious: Previous experience in a similar role in a higher-education environment in the disciplines of social sciences or humanities. International work experience Ability to communicate in multiple languages Other: The position is a special fixed-term employment of nine months, with a possible extension. The scope is between 50–100%, upon agreement. The role is based in Stockholm, and you are expected to work on-site. We encourage you to apply promptly as we are actively reviewing applications on an ongoing basis. Please be aware that we conduct background checks on final candidates for this position. About the Stockholm School of Economics The Stockholm School of Economics is ranked as the top business school in the Nordic and Baltic countries and enjoys a strong international reputation. World-class research forms the foundation of our educational offering, which includes Bachelor, Master, PhD, MBA, and Executive Education programs. Through creativity and collaboration, the Stockholm School of Economics provides an environment where ambitious students and accomplished researchers meet to address contemporary challenges within business and economics, particularly those concerning sustainability, diversity and innovation. Apart from delivering world class education within business and economics, SSE students are trained to be successful decision makers and leaders of the future. Our educational mission has over the years strengthened SSE students, and you can read more about it here. SSE is a member of the Stockholm Dual Career Network (SDCN) , a collaboration between universities, research institutes and companies in the Stockholm region. Through SDCN, partners of international recruits are offered professional support in establishing their careers in Sweden, including career coaching, networking opportunities, seminars and access to a broad professional network. We recognize the importance of supporting accompanying partners in international relocations and are committed to facilitating a smooth transition for the whole family. SSE is committed to a balanced gender distribution and values a variety of backgrounds and experiences among our employees. We therefore welcome all applicants regardless of their gender, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, disability, sexual orientation, age, or religion or other beliefs. We strive to have a fair and inclusive recruitment process. Type of employment Special fixed-term employment Contract type Full-time/Part-time First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 50-100% City Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number 2026/56 Contact Ellen Falkenström Published 11.Sep.2026 Last application date 27.Sep.2026 11:59 PM CEST Share links Apply for position A career page by Grade Varbi × We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here"
    },
    "http://jobs.hhs.se/en/job/stockholm/program_manager_to_sse_executive_education_-968841.html": {
      "title": "Program Manager to SSE Executive Education",
      "description": "Program Manager to SSE Executive Education Available Positions Departments Back Program Manager to SSE Executive Education Executive Education SSE Executive Education is a fully-owned subsidiary of the Stockholm School of Economics and the leading partner for executive education in Northern Europe. It is ranked as the best in the Nordic region for leadership and business development according to the Financial Times. Here, academic research is integrated with the business world. SSE Executive Education develops leaders with a focus on specialized areas such as innovation and entrepreneurship, sustainable growth, and financial economics, enhancing the competitiveness of companies, organizations, and the public sector through powerful transformation. About the Position We are looking for a Program Manager for the SSE MBA program at the Stockholm School of Economics. You will be employed by SSE Executive Education, a fully owned subsidiary of the Stockholm School of Economics and the leading partner for executive education in Northern Europe situated in Stockholm. You will be part of the SSE MBA Team and together you will work with delivering high-quality education in various formats. As Program Manager, you will be involved in everything from preparation and planning, administration, program support and follow-up. Travelling, both within and outside of Sweden, is a part of the role and includes about two long-distance trips annually. Occasionally you will also be working with alumni activities and events, as well as other Executive Education programs You will be offered: A stimulating learning environment where you will interact with both Swedish and international clients, participants, and faculty. The opportunity to develop professionally and be a key figure in the preparation, execution, and follow-up of various types of programs, both physical and digital. To be a part of a small company in an exciting environment closely connected to the academic world, where you have the opportunity to influence and are expected to take personal responsibility and initiative for your own development, as well as for others and the business. Responsibilities: As a Program Manager, you will be responsible for coordinating, organizing, and assisting in the daily operations of programs delivered in Sweden, abroad, and on digital platforms. You will, among other things: Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Actively taking part in pre-sales activities together with the Account Managers in your team. Registering students, creating as well as running the program website, ensuring pedagogical structure is followed and content updated. Planning and contributing to the implementation of both live and online modules, webinars and pure online training. Supporting colleagues and faculty with digital matters. Actively taking part in all campus weeks, working closely with the Program Director, faculty, and participants to ensure quality. Evaluating programs during implementation and after completion. Handling the grading process. Managing program administration as well as invoicing and budget follow-up. Being responsible for external communication with both participants and external clients. Your profile You are likely to be described as a service-minded organizer with strong collaborative and communications skills. You enjoy working in a high-tempo environment, both independently and together with others, and you can easily adapt to changing circumstances. You are proactive, have strong problem-solving skills and an eye for details. When needed, you are decisive and action oriented. You are warm, open, and enjoy interacting with people. Requirements: A few years of experience from similar work areas. Experience leading and managing your own projects. Excellent technical- and system knowledge. Excellent oral and written communication skills in English and Swedish, and the ability to communicate in a pedagogical way. Interest in and ability to travel short and long distances in Sweden and abroad Additional Information: Start date to be determined by mutual agreement. We look forward to receiving your application, CV, and cover letter by October 8 at the latest, in which you describe your relevant experience and why you are a suitable candidate for this role. We encourage you to apply promptly as we are actively reviewing applications on an ongoing basis. If you have any questions about the position, feel free to contact Emma Hellsten (HR Business Partner) at emma.hellsten@hhs.se SSE Executive MBA: Degree programs for leaders Located in Stockholm, Sweden - a global hub for innovation, entrepreneurship, and sustainable business - SSE is at the forefront of developing forward-thinking leaders. Our Executive MBA programs are part of the degree offering at SSE although for working executives and leaders. The programs are built on a general management foundation but focus on different participants and content. The SSE MBA Executive Format focuses on leaders who want to shape organizations and drive impact across industries worldwide. The SSE Nordic Defense MBA, in collaboration with the Swedish Armed Forces, focuses on leaders with a total defense interest. Both programs are international and take participants to different parts of the world and partner schools. About Stockholm School of Economics The Stockholm School of Economics is ranked as the top business school in the Nordic and Baltic countries and enjoys a strong international reputation. World-class research forms the foundation of our educational offering, which includes Bachelor, Master, PhD, MBA, and Executive Education programs. Through creativity and collaboration, the Stockholm School of Economics provides an environment where ambitious students and accomplished researchers meet to address contemporary challenges within business and economics, particularly those concerning sustainability, diversity and innovation. Apart from delivering world class education within business and economics, SSE students are trained to be successful decision makers and leaders of the future. Our educational mission has over the years strengthened SSE students, and you can read more about it here. SSE is a member of the Stockholm Dual Career Network (SDCN) , a collaboration between universities, research institutes and companies in the Stockholm region. Through SDCN, partners of international recruits are offered professional support in establishing their careers in Sweden, including career coaching, networking opportunities, seminars and access to a broad professional network. We recognize the importance of supporting accompanying partners in international relocations and are committed to facilitating a smooth transition for the whole family. SSE is committed to a balanced gender distribution and values a variety of backgrounds and experiences among our employees. We therefore welcome all applicants regardless of their gender, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, disability, sexual orientation, age, or religion or other beliefs. We strive to have a fair and inclusive recruitment process. Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number 2026/59 Contact Emma Hellsten, 08-7369000 Published 11.Sep.2026 Last application date 08.Oct.2026 11:59 PM CEST Share links Apply for position A career page by Grade Varbi × We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here"
    },
    "http://jobs.hhs.se/en/job/stockholm/project_manager_to_the_center_for_security_and_resilience-966613.html": {
      "title": "Project Manager to the Center for Security and Resilience",
      "description": "Project Manager to the Center for Security and Resilience Available Positions Departments Back Project Manager to the Center for Security and Resilience CfSR The Center for Security and Resilience is seeking a motivated and organized Project Manager who can take ownership of projects from initial concept and planning through implementation, evaluation, and continued development. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys working with a wide range of stakeholders and combining strategic development with hands-on execution. A key part of the role involves planning and delivering both academic and practitioner-focused events, as well as recruiting and engaging students and hourly employees for various projects and assignments. About the Center for Security and Resilience Building security through competitiveness. In a world shaped by disruption, agile competitiveness is increasingly central to national and global security. The Center for Security and Resilience (CfSR) brings together academia, business, and government to explore how societies can grow stronger in preparing for and managing crises and war. About the Role As Project Manager, you will have broad responsibility for planning, coordinating, and delivering activities at the Center for Security and Resilience. You will oversee projects as a whole, create structure, and ensure that objectives are achieved on time and within budget. You will work closely with students, partner organizations, and other relevant stakeholders. The role includes both independent work and collaboration with internal and external stakeholders. You will report to the Executive Director of the Center for Security and Resilience. Your primary responsibilities will include, but not be limited to: Managing projects from start to finish, from needs assessment and project planning through implementation, monitoring, and evaluation Planning and delivering seminars, conferences, workshops, networking events, and other activities Recruiting, onboarding, and coordinating research assistants for various projects and assignments Developing clear processes for recruitment, staffing, onboarding, and event management Creating project timelines, assigning responsibilities, preparing budgets, and establishing monitoring procedures Coordinating participants, speakers, vendors, and partner organizations Preparing information, instructions, and other materials for projects and activities Ensuring a professional participant experience before, during, and after each event or activity Reviewing existing processes, documenting outcomes, and developing improved ways of working based on feedback Contributing to the development of the Center’s operations, procedures, and long-term partnerships Your profile We are looking for someone who is proactive, solutions-oriented, and skilled at bringing structure to projects with many moving parts. You take ownership of your work and can shift between long-term planning and hands-on tasks as needed. You are organized and structured in your work, while remaining flexible, service-oriented and confident in leading, coordinating, and supporting others to achieve shared goals. To succeed in this role, you should be a clear, confident, and engaging communicator who can build trust, align stakeholders, and translate complex information into practical guidance for different audiences. Requirements: A relevant academic degree or equivalent professional experience Experience independently planning, managing, and completing projects Experience organizing events, large-scale programs, or similar activities Experience recruiting, staffing, or coordinating employees, students, or volunteers Strong administrative skills and ability to create structure, manage details, and keep projects organized and on track Experience developing and quality-assuring procedures, instructions, and work processes Swedish and English Meritorious: Experience working with student programs, professional development, training initiatives, digital learning platforms, or topics related to security, emergency preparedness, and resilience is a plus What We Offer At the Center for Security and Resilience, you will have a varied role with significant responsibility and the opportunity to influence how the Center and its projects develop. You will work in an environment where knowledge, civic engagement, and practical implementation come together, with students and external stakeholders serving as key partners. Other: This is a full-time, permanent position with an initial six-month probationary period. The position is located in Stockholm and start date according to agreement. We encourage you to apply promptly as we are actively reviewing applications on an ongoing basis. Please be aware that we conduct background checks on final candidates for this position. About the Stockholm School of Economics The Stockholm School of Economics is ranked as the top business school in the Nordic and Baltic countries and enjoys a strong international reputation. World-class research forms the foundation of our educational offering, which includes Bachelor, Master, PhD, MBA, and Executive Education programs. Through creativity and collaboration, the Stockholm School of Economics provides an environment where ambitious students and accomplished researchers meet to address contemporary challenges within business and economics, particularly those concerning sustainability, diversity and innovation. Apart from delivering world class education within business and economics, SSE students are trained to be successful decision makers and leaders of the future. Our educational mission has over the years strengthened SSE students, and you can read more about it here. SSE is a member of the Stockholm Dual Career Network (SDCN) , a collaboration between universities, research institutes and companies in the Stockholm region. Through SDCN, partners of international recruits are offered professional support in establishing their careers in Sweden, including career coaching, networking opportunities, seminars and access to a broad professional network. We recognize the importance of supporting accompanying partners in international relocations and are committed to facilitating a smooth transition for the whole family. SSE is committed to a balanced gender distribution and values a variety of backgrounds and experiences among our employees. We therefore welcome all applicants regardless of their gender, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, disability, sexual orientation, age, or religion or other beliefs. We strive to have a fair and inclusive recruitment process. Type of employment Permanent position – (starting with a temporary contract) Contract type Full time First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number 2026/55 Contact Staffan Holmberg Ellen Falkenström Published 08.Sep.2026 Last application date 29.Sep.2026 11:59 PM CEST Share links Apply for position A career page by Grade Varbi × We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here"
    },
    "http://jobs.hhs.se/en/job/stockholm/project_manager_including_european_degree_development_to_civica_at_the_stockholm_school_of_economics-968344.html": {
      "title": "Project Manager including European Degree development to CIVICA",
      "description": "Project Manager including European Degree development to CIVICA at the Stockholm School of Economics Available Positions Departments Back Project Manager including European Degree development to CIVICA at the Stockholm School of Economics Education Office The Education Office (EdO) is one of SSE’s Professional Services units and consists of around 58 colleagues. As a central part of the SSE journey, we support and develop key academic services for students and stakeholders across our BSc, MSc, and PhD programs. Our work spans assessment, program management, scholarships, international collaborations, academic support, central course and exam coordination, as well as degrees and certificates. About CIVICA CIVICA – The European University of Social Science- is since 2019 a European Universities Alliance funded under the Erasmus+ program, aimed at implementing and developing new forms of partnerships with nine other European universities in the field of social sciences. As the CIVICA Manager, your role is twofold (1) to be the main liaison and actor for SSE’s activities internally and towards the CIVICA network (2) to lead the exploration and preparation work to transform the CIVICA Engage Track into a European Joint Bachelor’s degree.  The ambition is to prepare the ground for a future European Bachelor’s Degree (label) . If the initiative is successful, a program manager will be recruited in the future. SSE is one of CIVICA’s founding members with Sciences Po (the alliance coordinator, France), Bocconi (Italy), The London School of Economics and Political Science (United Kingdom), Central European University (Austria and Hungary), European University Institute (Florence), Hertie School (Germany), National University of Political Studies and Public Administration (Romania), SGH Warsaw School of Economics (Poland) and IE University (Spain). Since 2019, CIVICA members have jointly developed innovative activities in education, research, outreach and civic engagement; the alliance is currently in the process of developing its long-term vision and inscription in the European Degree landscape. We offer you a management role in the CIVICA project, an international and effervescent environment, at one of the top business schools in Europe. Within the CIVICA network, you will successfully manage a strategic interplay with international key stakeholders (Higher Education Institutions, Students, corporate and societal partners) to drive and develop the CIVICA project further.  The role is positioned within our Education Office department. The role Your tasks will include, but not be limited to: Manage and lead all activities related to the implementation of the CIVICA project at SSE, such as: Identify and serve the needs of SSE’s CIVICA operations in the various work packages, in line with SSE’s international strategy. Track milestones, tasks and deliverables and be responsible for SSE’s reporting to CIVICA, Budget and financial tracking of all CIVICA operations at SSE, Be part of several work packages to guarantee progress of SSE’s CIVICA operations, including WP1, governance, Hosting and leading in-person and online meetings internally and externally. Lead the exploration and preparation work to transform the CIVICA Engage Track into a European Joint Bachelor’s degree: Become SSE’s expert on European Degree (label) by following all developments on the topic at the European level Understand the work that other European University Alliances have done to deliver European Degree (label) Establish a value proposition for the Engage Track to be transformed into a European Degree (label) for all CIVICA partners Establish a road map and plan for a pilot to transform the Engage Track into a Joint European Degree (label) in a very near future Your profile Used to being responsible for multiple processes you are well-organized as well as proactive, creative, and flexible. You thrive in emerging projects where routines and solutions need to be invented while navigating established demanding structures. You are comfortable moving projects forward, and get things done efficiently and accurately. You are self-confident and independent, used to working inclusively in diverse and international teams to achieve high goals. You are service-minded and confident in dealing with a variety of stakeholders to advance the project you represent. Qualifications Experience of successful international project management, in particular Erasmus+ or Horizon Europe Experience in the European higher education sector in developing or implementing a joint or double degree program, for example, as program manager English Meritorious: Previous experience in a similar role in a higher-education environment in the disciplines of social sciences or humanities. International work experience Ability to communicate in multiple languages Other: The position is a special fixed-term employment of nine months, with a possible extension. The scope is between 50–100%, upon agreement. The role is based in Stockholm, and you are expected to work on-site. We encourage you to apply promptly as we are actively reviewing applications on an ongoing basis. Please be aware that we conduct background checks on final candidates for this position. About the Stockholm School of Economics The Stockholm School of Economics is ranked as the top business school in the Nordic and Baltic countries and enjoys a strong international reputation. World-class research forms the foundation of our educational offering, which includes Bachelor, Master, PhD, MBA, and Executive Education programs. Through creativity and collaboration, the Stockholm School of Economics provides an environment where ambitious students and accomplished researchers meet to address contemporary challenges within business and economics, particularly those concerning sustainability, diversity and innovation. Apart from delivering world class education within business and economics, SSE students are trained to be successful decision makers and leaders of the future. Our educational mission has over the years strengthened SSE students, and you can read more about it here. SSE is a member of the Stockholm Dual Career Network (SDCN) , a collaboration between universities, research institutes and companies in the Stockholm region. Through SDCN, partners of international recruits are offered professional support in establishing their careers in Sweden, including career coaching, networking opportunities, seminars and access to a broad professional network. We recognize the importance of supporting accompanying partners in international relocations and are committed to facilitating a smooth transition for the whole family. SSE is committed to a balanced gender distribution and values a variety of backgrounds and experiences among our employees. We therefore welcome all applicants regardless of their gender, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, disability, sexual orientation, age, or religion or other beliefs. We strive to have a fair and inclusive recruitment process. Type of employment Special fixed-term employment Contract type Full-time/Part-time First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 50-100% City Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number 2026/56 Contact Ellen Falkenström Published 11.Sep.2026 Last application date 27.Sep.2026 11:59 PM CEST Share links Apply for position A career page by Grade Varbi × We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here"
